Essentially, I don't play any conducts.  Most conducts are doable for 
any seasoned player, if he/she is willing to expend enough characters in 
the attempt...  No real challenge, just throwing dice long enough to 
become lucky.

Not killing a priest as a lawful or neutral is just a means of avoiding 
the loss of telepathy.  (In addition, trying to act lawfully as a lawful 
is just role-playing.)

If you have followed the thread before, you must have seen that I was 
talking about an early-game character, one for whom an altar would be a 
real boon.  A character who has a pet that is strong enough to take out 
a priest does not really need an altar that badly. He can just descend a 
little further.  But for an early-game character, telepathy is so 
important for survival that he simply cannot afford to give it away just 
to kill a priest by himself.
